https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IvjOnKqubJU  (Capo 4)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

A version in D follows which may be slightly easier to play but is capo'd too high to sing along with the recording.

TIP:  The (G/F3) (F3/C) sequence is very easy to play.  Play that (G/F3) as an (F) on the 3rd fret, but notice the extra finger (pinky) covering the bass note above the ring finger on the 5th string/5th fret.  Now after the (G/F3) will always come the (F3/C) so all you do is take that pinky from the 5th string above the ring finger to the 3rd string below the ring finger.  Your other fingers keep the (F) formation (the pinky will cancel out the ring finger).  Easy-peasy.  Down/up.  Also note that this sequence appears in the first and last chorus in which the lead-in on "Don't you think it's time?" so be ready for it. 

TIP:  The last line of the song is repeated in the same melody as the line that preceded it.


